  <data key="d7">Strong metal-support interaction at the Ru/W18O49 interface produces an electron-deficient Ru cluster state, modulates Ru–H strength, and, together with proton transport through W18O49, enables efficient bifunctional hydrogen electrocatalysis.</data>
  <data key="d8">mixed</data>
  <data key="d9">Mechanistic interpretation explicitly attributed to microstructural analyses, X-ray absorption spectroscopy, and DFT calculations.</data>
  <data key="d10">["claim_mechanism_1"]</data>
  <data key="d11">1</data>
